Chapter: ListInduction

 The second route: induction over the BUILTIN List. The
 induction checker resolves `xs : List a` to a synthesized Nil/Cons
 view, and the proof normalizer reduces the builtin primitives
 (list-length, list-push, list-snoc, list-at) over Nil/Cons spines.
 Before this, every such claim was accepted as an unproven axiom with
 CDX4022; this file must compile with ZERO CDX4022 and zero errors,
 and the negative guards live in codex/test/errors/list-induction-false
 and codex/test/errors/list-prim-false, where a false claim over the
 same shapes must be a hard error.

Section: Inductions

  claim len-push : for all (xs : List Integer), list-length (list-push xs 7) === 1 + list-length xs
  proof len-push =
   induction on xs
    is Nil -> Refl
    is Cons (h) (t) (ih) -> cong ih
   qed

  claim len-snoc : for all (xs : List Integer), list-length (list-snoc xs 3) === 1 + list-length xs
  proof len-snoc =
   induction on xs
    is Nil -> Refl
    is Cons (h) (t) (ih) -> cong ih
   qed

  claim len-append : for all (xs : List Integer), list-length (xs & Cons 7 Nil) === 1 + list-length xs
  proof len-append =
   induction on xs
    is Nil -> Refl
    is Cons (h) (t) (ih) -> cong ih
   qed

Section: Primitive Reductions

 Ground claims with no induction, each discharged by Refl only because
 the normalizer actually reduces the primitive: at 0 is the head, at 1
 recurses into the tail, and push walks to the end.

  claim at-head : list-at (Cons 5 Nil) 0 === 5
  proof at-head = Refl
  qed

  claim at-second : list-at (Cons 5 (Cons 6 Nil)) 1 === 6
  proof at-second = Refl
  qed

  claim push-shape : list-push (Cons 1 Nil) 2 === Cons 1 (Cons 2 Nil)
  proof push-shape = Refl
  qed

 A later pass carried the remaining three primitives here. Each ground
 claim below is discharged by Refl only because its rule fires; without
 the rule the spine stays stuck and the claim is a CDX2001 mismatch,
 which is what makes these a test rather than a decoration.

  claim set-head : list-set-at (Cons 5 (Cons 6 Nil)) 0 9 === Cons 9 (Cons 6 Nil)
  proof set-head = Refl
  qed

  claim set-second : list-set-at (Cons 5 (Cons 6 Nil)) 1 9 === Cons 5 (Cons 9 Nil)
  proof set-second = Refl
  qed

  claim insert-front : list-insert-at (Cons 5 Nil) 0 9 === Cons 9 (Cons 5 Nil)
  proof insert-front = Refl
  qed

  claim insert-into-nil : list-insert-at Nil 0 9 === Cons 9 Nil
  proof insert-into-nil = Refl
  qed

  claim insert-mid : list-insert-at (Cons 5 (Cons 6 Nil)) 1 9 === Cons 5 (Cons 9 (Cons 6 Nil))
  proof insert-mid = Refl
  qed

  claim append-nil : Nil & Cons 2 Nil === Cons 2 Nil
  proof append-nil = Refl
  qed

  claim append-shape : Cons 1 Nil & Cons 2 Nil === Cons 1 (Cons 2 Nil)
  proof append-shape = Refl
  qed

Section: Main

 The proofs erase at emit, so the runtime line is what the battery can
 see; the compile-time content is the zero-CDX4022 requirement above.

  opening : [Console] Nothing
  opening = act
   print-line-uni "list-induction: QED"
  end
